  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Right-angled triangles via Pythagoras and SOH-CAH-TOA, then any triangle through the sine and cosine rules. Bearings questions are trigonometry in disguise — always start with a clear diagram.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Definition 6.1 — Right-triangle ratios",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "For an acute angle \\( \\theta \\) in a right triangle, \\( \\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{\\text{opp}}{\\text{hyp}} \\), \\( \\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{\\text{adj}}{\\text{hyp}} \\), \\( \\tan\\theta=\\dfrac{\\text{opp}}{\\text{adj}} \\) — the rule remembered as <strong>SOH-CAH-TOA</strong>.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Drag the angle and watch the three ratios respond. The hypotenuse is fixed in length; the opposite and adjacent sides — and the ratios built from them — change together.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · The trig ratios",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "trigCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A right triangle with adjustable angle theta, showing opposite, adjacent and hypotenuse",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "trigDataBtn",
          "panelId": "trigDataPanel",
          "descId": "trigDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "trigDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "The current triangle's sides and trig ratios",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "quantity",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "value",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "trigAngle",
            "label": {
              "en": "Angle &nbsp; <b>θ =</b>",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 10,
            "max": 80,
            "value": 35,
            "step": 1,
            "valueDisplayId": "trigA",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Angle θ",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "trigSin",
            "label": {
              "en": "sin θ",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "indigo",
            "value": "—"
          },
          {
            "id": "trigCos",
            "label": {
              "en": "cos θ",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "indigo",
            "value": "—"
          },
          {
            "id": "trigTan",
            "label": {
              "en": "tan θ",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "amber",
            "value": "—"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "Opposite &amp; adjacent are drawn in indigo, the hypotenuse in amber. As \\( \\theta\\to 90^{\\circ} \\), \\( \\tan\\theta \\) grows without bound.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Pythagoras",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( a^{2}+b^{2}=c^{2} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Sine rule",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{a}{\\sin A}=\\dfrac{b}{\\sin B}=\\dfrac{c}{\\sin C} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Cosine rule",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( c^{2}=a^{2}+b^{2}-2ab\\cos C \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Triangle area",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\tfrac12\\,ab\\sin C \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 6.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A right triangle has hypotenuse \\( 10 \\) and an angle of \\( 30^{\\circ} \\). Find the side opposite that angle.</p>\\[ \\text{opp}=10\\sin 30^{\\circ}=10\\times 0.5=5. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 6.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>In a triangle, \\( a=7 \\), \\( b=8 \\) and the included angle \\( C=60^{\\circ} \\). Find \\( c \\).</p><p>Apply the cosine rule with \\( \\cos 60^{\\circ}=0.5 \\):</p>\\[ c^{2}=49+64-2(7)(8)(0.5)=57,\\qquad c=\\sqrt{57}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Bearings",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "A <strong>bearing</strong> is a clockwise angle measured from North, always written as a three-digit number (e.g. 045°, 270°). Draw a North line at the starting point, then measure clockwise. The bearing from B back to A is the <strong>back-bearing</strong> = bearing ± 180°.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 6.C — Bearings with trig",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A ship sails 40 km on a bearing of 130° from port P. How far east and south of P is it?</p><p>East component: \\(40\\sin50°\\approx30.6\\) km. &nbsp; South component: \\(40\\cos50°\\approx25.7\\) km.</p><p>(Angle from South = 180°−130° = 50°.)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● 3D Trigonometry <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span>",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Identify a right-angled triangle within the 3D figure: find a face diagonal using Pythagoras, then use that as one side of a second right triangle. The <strong>angle of elevation</strong> is measured upward from horizontal; the <strong>angle of depression</strong> downward from horizontal.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Back-bearing",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "bearing \\(\\pm180°\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "3D diagonal",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(\\sqrt{l^2+w^2+h^2}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Angle of elevation",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "upward from horizontal",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Angle of depression",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "downward from horizontal",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 6.D — 3D trig <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span>",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A cuboid has length 8 cm, width 6 cm, height 3 cm. Find the angle the space diagonal makes with the base.</p><p>Base diagonal \\(=\\sqrt{8^2+6^2}=10\\) cm.</p>\\[\\tan\\theta=\\frac{3}{10}\\;\\Rightarrow\\;\\theta=\\arctan(0.3)\\approx16.7°.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "A tower PQ stands vertically. From point A on level ground, 50 m from the base Q, the angle of elevation of P is 32°. Find the height of the tower.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(h=50\\tan32°\\approx50\\times0.6249\\approx31.2\\) m.",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
